1
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:48,009
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:51,050
[Episode 9]

3
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:52,930
Alright,

4
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:54,000
if there are

5
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,979
no other questions,

6
00:01:54,979 --> 00:01:56,370
let's end today's meeting here.

7
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:57,780
If you come up with any new plans

8
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,430
or ideas,

9
00:01:58,430 --> 00:02:00,090
feel free to email me anytime.

10
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:00,710
Okay.

11
00:02:00,710 --> 00:02:01,840
Meeting adjourned.

12
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,400
Mr. Qin,

13
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,430
I genuinely think

14
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:13,180
the flash mob you proposed...

15
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:15,470
Yun Li,

16
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:17,079
was the guy looking for you

17
00:02:17,079 --> 00:02:18,480
just now your boyfriend?

18
00:02:20,090 --> 00:02:21,090
Of course not.

19
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:22,430
He's just a young friend of mine.

20
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:23,290
A young friend?

21
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:24,870
Is he that young?

22
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:26,010
Still in school?

23
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,300
He's from NUST.

24
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:28,590
From the same school as you?

25
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:29,990
Are you in the same class?

26
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:32,190
Yun Li, come here for a second.

27
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:33,620
I've got to go.

28
00:02:57,740 --> 00:02:59,000
S-Sorry. I'm so sorry.

29
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:01,180
This is the coffee
my boss asked me to grab.

30
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,000
What now?

31
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:02,930
Sorry,

32
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:04,390
let me buy you another one.

33
00:03:05,130 --> 00:03:05,930
Never mind.

34
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:07,500
Don't bother.

35
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,240
That won't do.

36
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,340
I made you spill it. I'll pay.

37
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:11,870
You're so nice.

38
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:13,740
How about...

39
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:16,579
you just transfer me
the money for the coffee?

40
00:03:16,579 --> 00:03:17,370
Okay.

41
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,260
Let's add each other on WeChat.

42
00:03:20,690 --> 00:03:23,490
Actually,
there's no need to go to so much trouble.

43
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,540
A payment code will do.

44
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,190
You don't look

45
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,900
like an employee here.

46
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,240
Are you here to negotiate business?

47
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,640
I'm here to meet someone.

48
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,090
I just saw you talking

49
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:38,970
to Mr. Xu.

50
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:40,630
Are you two...

51
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,240
He's my brother.

52
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:43,210
I've transferred

53
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:44,060
30 yuan to you.

54
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:44,750
Sorry about that.

55
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:45,280
Bye-bye.

56
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:54,360
"Fu Zhengchu"?

57
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,470
Hello, welcome.

58
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,090
It's done.

59
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:03,960
Let me see.

60
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:10,910
Why do you want to choose science?

61
00:04:12,510 --> 00:04:13,620
When I was little,

62
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:15,490
my sister often took me to XUST,

63
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,390
and I watched the students

64
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:17,269
play with drones.

65
00:04:17,269 --> 00:04:19,220
I found drones super-duper cool.

66
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:21,450
That's why I want to choose science

67
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:22,450
and get into XUST.

68
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,360
I also think drones are cool.

69
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,570
But actually, I'm jealous

70
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:29,370
that you can go study abroad.

71
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:33,000
That way, you don't have to take
the college entrance exam.

72
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:37,060
Honestly,
I don't really want to study abroad.

73
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:39,159
It's all my family's arrangement.

74
00:04:39,159 --> 00:04:40,500
Going abroad,

75
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,560
there's nothing I'm familiar with.

76
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:44,270
With my personality,

77
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:46,400
I'm not good at making friends either.

78
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:49,950
It's... It's okay.

79
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,360
After a while,

80
00:04:51,450 --> 00:04:52,950
you'll naturally
get to know people, right?

81
00:04:52,950 --> 00:04:54,750
Just like we do now?

82
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,720
Thanks.

83
00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:17,240
Are you stargazing?

84
00:05:18,870 --> 00:05:20,430
I love stargazing.

85
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,130
Did you know?

86
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:23,180
There are

87
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:24,830
6,974 stars we can see

88
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,740
with the naked eye from Earth.

89
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,340
Have you counted them?

90
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,000
What's your zodiac sign?

91
00:05:32,010 --> 00:05:32,950
Cancer.

92
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:37,920
What about you?

93
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,930
What's yours?

94
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:42,240
Mine is over there.

95
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:47,720
I can't tell the shape.

96
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,720
So what's your zodiac sign?

97
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,010
I'll tell you in the future.

98
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:55,240
I think you should apply

99
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,770
for the astronomy program.

100
00:05:56,810 --> 00:05:58,920
Forget about what I'm going to apply for.

101
00:05:58,920 --> 00:05:59,830
You should worry about

102
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,330
your next monthly exam.

103
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:02,420
I'm not worried at all.

104
00:06:02,420 --> 00:06:02,950
I...

105
00:06:06,710 --> 00:06:07,800
If I

106
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:09,430
score better next time,

107
00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:10,690
will there be a reward?

108
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:16,450
You'll know after the exam.

109
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:18,100
Fine.

110
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:36,370
Mr. Qin,

111
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,920
I've been racking my brain
for quite a while,

112
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,590
but still can't come up with anything.

113
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:40,890
It's driving me crazy.

114
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,480
I'm merely a content creator

115
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,250
in dance.

116
00:06:43,370 --> 00:06:45,040
Making promotional plans

117
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,770
is really not my thing.

118
00:06:47,310 --> 00:06:48,510
You're experienced.

119
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:49,830
Please enlighten me.

120
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,720
Feifei,

121
00:06:51,130 --> 00:06:52,920
you're just too naive.

122
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,580
To climb up the social ladder,

123
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,040
you should learn to use tools!

124
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:58,870
Tools?

125
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,370
Mr. Qin,

126
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,570
please don't keep me in suspense.

127
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:07,570
It's about leveraging others' strength.

128
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,480
Look at me.

129
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,100
I didn't get where I am today

130
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,510
by doing everything

131
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:14,010
on my own.

132
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:15,620
People who want to prove themselves

133
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:17,220
will do their best,

134
00:07:17,430 --> 00:07:18,430
and we can just sit back

135
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:20,120
and reap the rewards.

136
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:23,730
I got it.

137
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:25,270
You're my cousin.

138
00:07:25,430 --> 00:07:26,770
Even if your plan

139
00:07:26,770 --> 00:07:27,980
isn't approved,

140
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:29,330
it doesn't matter.

141
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:30,980
The regular position

142
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:32,930
is definitely yours.

143
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,070
Mr. Qin,

144
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,120
you're taking such good care of me.

145
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,980
I'll definitely tell my mom about it.

146
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,980
We're family. Don't mention it.

147
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,330
What's wrong?

148
00:07:57,330 --> 00:07:58,540
Why the long face?

149
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:00,920
Tell me what happened.

150
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,180
I've got your back.

151
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:07,810
Well, the Light Chaser is about to launch.

152
00:08:07,810 --> 00:08:08,540
Our company

153
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:09,680
asked me to come up
with a promotional plan,

154
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,770
but I have no idea where to start.

155
00:08:11,770 --> 00:08:12,810
The Light Chaser?

156
00:08:13,810 --> 00:08:15,670
Is it the one invented by Fu Shize?

157
00:08:16,330 --> 00:08:17,660
Just ask him to help you.

158
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,730
The two of us are not

159
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:24,050
that close yet.

160
00:08:24,330 --> 00:08:26,870
You guys even held hands,

161
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:28,470
and you say you're not close?

162
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:31,040
How did you know?

163
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:33,750
Fu Zhengchu claimed

164
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,650
that he could keep a secret!

165
00:08:36,370 --> 00:08:38,000
I saw it.

166
00:08:38,030 --> 00:08:39,200
You saw it?

167
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:46,500
So last night, you and Fu Zhengchu

168
00:08:47,050 --> 00:08:48,500
both came across

169
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,700
Fu Shize and me...

170
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:52,100
You guys went on a date?

171
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:54,750
Nope,

172
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:55,550
we didn't.

173
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:56,790
Don't talk nonsense.

174
00:09:02,910 --> 00:09:03,720
Tang Lin,

175
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:06,390
if you don't tell me the truth,

176
00:09:07,010 --> 00:09:08,540
I'm going to interview you.

177
00:09:11,710 --> 00:09:14,120
We happened
to run into each other at dinner.

178
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,200
Nanwu is such a small place.

179
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:18,750
It's normal
to run into each other at dinner.

180
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,530
You ran into each other?

181
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:23,350
Then why are you blushing?

182
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,410
A girl's blush

183
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:25,700
reveals everything.

184
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,650
It's too hot.

185
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:28,360
Hot.

186
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:30,750
Fine,

187
00:09:30,890 --> 00:09:31,910
you ran into each other.

188
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:33,200
Whatever you say.

189
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:39,420
Weren't we talking about you?

190
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:41,320
How did it become about me?

191
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:42,390
Me?

192
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:45,820
Does that guy

193
00:09:46,290 --> 00:09:47,360
have pecs?

194
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:48,500
Pecs?

195
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,150
W-What pecs?

196
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:52,200
Fu Shize hugged you!

197
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,100
Didn't you...

198
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,200
H-Hugged me?

199
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,010
That never happened!

200
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:57,150
Y-You're imagining things.

201
00:09:57,150 --> 00:09:58,630
If I'm imagining things,

202
00:09:58,630 --> 00:09:59,820
what actually happened?

203
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:00,910
You... If you keep doing this,

204
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:02,390
I-I'm leaving.

205
00:10:02,390 --> 00:10:03,120
Go ahead.

206
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,000
I...

207
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:04,890
Go.

208
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:08,700
I'll impose economic sanctions on you.

209
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,360
I'll eat some more before I leave.

210
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:14,100
Just listen to me.

211
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,290
Just ask Fu Shize to help you

212
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:18,220
with the promotional plan,

213
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:21,070
so you two...

214
00:10:22,250 --> 00:10:24,050
can get closer to each other.

215
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:29,650
Well, then,

216
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,890
I-I'll text him when I get back.

217
00:10:32,430 --> 00:10:34,050
You'll definitely back out
when you get back.

218
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:36,390
Text him right now in front of me.

219
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:41,320
Tangy...

220
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,030
Text him.

221
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:09,840
I'll go to the engineering department
to find you tomorrow.

222
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,740
I'd like to ask you for a favor.

223
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,050
I-I sent the message.

224
00:11:14,050 --> 00:11:15,250
Look, I t-texted him.

225
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:17,890
Eat up.

226
00:11:20,370 --> 00:11:20,960
Okay.

227
00:11:34,530 --> 00:11:35,580
Actually, friends

228
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:36,980
and a couple

229
00:11:37,410 --> 00:11:39,220
may seem to be worlds apart,

230
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,370
but sometimes,

231
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,690
there's just a thin line between them.

232
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:44,990
You're always so cold, like an iceberg.

233
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:46,910
Wouldn't that scare all the girls away?

234
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:48,480
As long as you want to change,

235
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,320
you can find

236
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:51,850
the missing piece of the puzzle
in your heart.

237
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:06,920
Good morning.

238
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:08,300
It's a sunny day today.

239
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:09,550
Hope your day

240
00:12:09,550 --> 00:12:10,940
is just as bright.

241
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:14,250
Hello.

242
00:13:23,910 --> 00:13:25,310
Something came up today.

243
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,030
I'm not going to the office.

244
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:39,670
I think

245
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:41,250
my proposal looks good.

246
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:42,510
What do you think?

247
00:13:42,510 --> 00:13:43,270
Then what should I do?

248
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:45,400
Are you guys discussing the proposal?

249
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:47,170
Have you come up with anything?

250
00:13:47,170 --> 00:13:48,630
Let me help you brainstorm.

251
00:13:48,630 --> 00:13:51,270
I... I haven't figured it out either.

252
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:58,360
Yun Li,

253
00:13:58,870 --> 00:14:00,600
have you decided what to write?

254
00:14:02,410 --> 00:14:04,070
I'm going to grab some coffee.

255
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:08,860
[EAW Light Chaser Promotional Plan]

256
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:26,150
It's too hard.

257
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:37,740
It's so bitter.

258
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:46,010
What happened?

259
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:48,410
Why is he not coming all of a sudden?

260
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:57,650
Could he be sick?

261
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:02,020
Could he have had an accident?

262
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,620
What are you thinking, Yun Li?

263
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:08,420
May good people be safe forever.

264
00:15:13,130 --> 00:15:15,030
Could it simply be that

265
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:17,490
he suddenly
didn't feel like coming to work?

266
00:15:42,390 --> 00:15:43,670
I'm off, Yun Li.

267
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,570
Bye-bye, Qianqian.

268
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,250
Bye-bye.

269
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,010
Yun Li, you're still not leaving?

270
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:53,670
Everyone else's clocked out.

271
00:15:53,810 --> 00:15:54,840
There's a flash mob

272
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:55,820
at Haitian Mall today.

273
00:15:55,820 --> 00:15:56,820
Want to go with me?

274
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,840
I'll get off work in a bit.

275
00:16:08,410 --> 00:16:10,100
You don't have

276
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,410
to work so hard for peanuts.

277
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:14,910
Don't you plan

278
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:16,110
to go to Haitian Mall?

279
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,010
You should go now,

280
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:18,940
or you'll be late for the flash mob.

281
00:16:21,870 --> 00:16:23,470
Who is she trying to impress?

282
00:16:23,510 --> 00:16:24,220
I wonder

283
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,820
if she's really working hard
or just faking it.

284
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,460
What a busy day.

285
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:37,390
You're off work?

286
00:16:41,630 --> 00:16:44,160
You... Didn't you say you weren't coming?

287
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:47,500
Have you eaten yet?

288
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:48,250
Nope.

289
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,060
Let me treat you to dinner.

290
00:16:52,350 --> 00:16:53,090
Consider it

291
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:56,650
an apology for missing our appointment.

292
